Baseline read confirms the defect is exactly at the producer predicate: `readModelInputPricing` rejects `cacheRead <= 0` before `computeInputCostUsd`, while the arithmetic already supports zero. The input-rate predicate is also currently `<= 0`; I’ll leave that meaning unchanged because a zero uncached-input price would make all input free and is not the authoritative cache-read case. I’m capturing the package baseline now.
